From: Lavender XNU bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] arm64/corecrypto: declare SHA2 for SHA256 assembly only

The Lavender machine profile deliberately targets generic ARMv8-A so that
unrelated translation units cannot acquire optional ISA instructions. This
assembly file explicitly implements SHA-256 using the ARMv8 SHA2 instruction
group; declare that extension locally for this assembly translation unit without changing
global CPU flags.

--- a/osfmk/arm64/corecrypto/sha256_compress_arm64.s
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/corecrypto/sha256_compress_arm64.s
@@ -121,5 +121,8 @@
 #if defined(__arm64__)
 
 #include "arm64_isa_compatibility.h"
 
+// This file's SHA-256 implementation uses the ARMv8 SHA2 extension.
+.arch armv8-a+sha2
+
 .subsections_via_symbols
